Hexyl v0.17.0 retains its MIT OR Apache-2.0 terms. LICENSE-MIT and
LICENSE-APACHE are staged unchanged. The embedded CP437 table has its own
permissive Delan Azabani notice; the embedded CP1047 table retains IBM's
EPL-1.0 notice. Complete table notices are retained in embedded-tables.rs and
the full source archive. These notices are not replaced by the top-level
project licence label.

terminal_size 0.4.0 is MIT OR Apache-2.0. Other Cargo crates retain their
individual terms; dependencies.json identifies the pinned releases and crate
checksums. sources.tar.xz contains their complete source and notices, including
build-only and unused target packages. Rust's static runtime notices and its
exact installation receipt are under rust/; SDK runtime notices are under sdk/.

Original Pyxis recipe, helper and documentation are MPL-2.0. Patches to Hexyl
retain Hexyl's upstream terms. The new terminal_size Pyxis backend and changes
to that crate use terminal_size's MIT OR Apache-2.0 terms.

Local changes:
- Replace Hexyl's sole libc ESPIPE use with std ErrorKind::NotSeekable and remove
  its direct libc dependency. Other locked package versions remain unchanged.
- Return input read failures instead of printing stale data or retrying forever;
  Interrupted reads retry. Explicitly flush final buffered output, including C
  include mode. Upstream BrokenPipe exit-success behavior remains.
- Select terminal_size's native Pyxis backend and restrict rustix to Unix targets.
  The backend calls the existing supplied-descriptor console-size C API, with
  no new kernel ABI, Unix impersonation or ambient terminal lookup. It checks
  stdout, stderr, stdin and rejects invalid or out-of-range dimensions.

The admitted invocation uses explicit --character-table=ascii. Box borders and
colours need terminal qualification. Default missing diamond/bullet glyphs,
networking, subprocesses and general crate portability are not promised.
